:: StoryInit
<<script>>
(function () {
  function notifyParent(event) {
    window.parent.postMessage(
      Object.assign({ source: 'choose-your-chaos' }, event),
      '*'
    );
  }

  $(document).on(':passagedisplay', function (event) {
    var passage = event.detail.passage;
    notifyParent({
      type: 'passage-displayed',
      passage: passage.name,
      tags: passage.tags || [],
      historyLength: State.length
    });
  });

  $(document).on('click', 'a[data-passage]', function () {
    notifyParent({
      type: 'choice-selected',
      targetPassage: this.getAttribute('data-passage') || '',
      label: (this.textContent || '').trim()
    });
  });

  $(document).one(':storyready', function () {
    notifyParent({ type: 'runtime-ready' });
  });
})();
<</script>>

:: Start [chapter]
<h1>The City That Forgot Dawn</h1>
<p>In Nera, every clock has stopped at 5:17. The sun has not risen for generations, and the city has learned to love its endless blue evening.</p>
<p>Tonight, a brass lantern appears on the abandoned station platform. A tiny golden star floats inside it.</p>
<p><em>Mara, the station keeper, watches the lantern flicker.</em></p>
<p>“It has chosen someone. I hope you know what to do with a little light.”</p>

[[Ask Mara about the missing sunrise->Mara]]
[[Follow the little blue light over the rooftops->Rooftops]]
[[Take the lantern and explore the night market->Market]]

:: Mara [chapter]
<h1>The Keeper's Secret</h1>
<p>Mara unlocks a room behind the station clock. Old timetables cover the walls. Every one ends on the same date: the Night of the Golden Festival.</p>
<p>“The Queen was afraid her happiest day would end,” Mara says. “So she asked the clockmaker to keep that evening forever.”</p>
<p>The lantern pulses. Somewhere beneath the city, something answers.</p>

[[Read the Queen's letter->Letter]]
[[Study the clockmaker's mechanism map->Mechanism]]

:: Rooftops [chapter]
<h1>Above the Sleeping City</h1>
<p>You climb a narrow staircase and find a small bird made of blue sparks. It circles the old bell tower, then flies toward a thin line of gold behind the mountains.</p>
<p>Morning is still out there. It has simply been held back.</p>

[[Follow the bird to the bell tower->BellTower]]
[[Return to the station and ask Mara for help->Mara]]

:: Market [chapter]
<h1>The Lantern Market</h1>
<p>A child named Lina is searching for a glass star that fell from her mother's necklace. The lantern glows when she tells you why it matters.</p>
<p>“My mother left to find the sunrise,” Lina says. “She promised she would come back when it returned.”</p>

[[Help Lina search the market->Lina]]
[[Follow the lantern's glow toward the river->River]]

:: Letter [chapter]
<h1>The Queen's Letter</h1>
<p>The Queen's letter describes a festival filled with music, warm bread, and a thousand paper stars above the river.</p>
<p>At the bottom, one sentence is underlined: “A beautiful moment is a gift because it ends, and makes room for another.”</p>

[[Take the letter to the clockmaker's tower->BellTower]]

:: Mechanism [chapter]
<h1>The Clockwork Heart</h1>
<p>The map reveals a hidden gear beneath the central clock. It is not broken. It is waiting for someone to turn it.</p>
<p>Three symbols are engraved beside the gear: memory, courage, and hope.</p>

[[Carry the map to the bell tower->BellTower]]

:: BellTower [chapter]
<h1>The Silent Bell</h1>
<p>The lantern's golden star rises into the bell. For the first time in years, the tower makes a sound.</p>
<p>Across Nera, windows open. People step outside and look toward the mountains.</p>

[[Climb to the clock face->ClockFace]]

:: Lina [chapter]
<h1>A Star Returned</h1>
<p>You find the glass star beneath a wooden stall. Lina holds it close, and the lantern fills with a second golden spark.</p>
<p>“Maybe the sunrise can find us now,” she whispers.</p>

[[Walk with Lina to the river->River]]

:: River [chapter]
<h1>Where the City Remembers</h1>
<p>Paper lanterns drift along the river. Their reflections look like a thousand small mornings.</p>
<p>The current carries the lantern toward the central clock tower.</p>

[[Follow the river to the clock tower->ClockFace]]

:: ClockFace [chapter]
<h1>The Last Choice Before Dawn</h1>
<p>At the heart of the clock, you find the Queen's final mechanism. The lantern floats beside three empty spaces.</p>
<p>One asks you to preserve the festival forever. One asks you to let the memories go. The last asks you to share the light with everyone in Nera.</p>

[[Keep the perfect evening forever->EndingStillness]]
[[Release the spell and welcome change->EndingMorning]]
[[Give the lantern to the people of Nera->EndingTogether]]

:: EndingStillness [ending]
<h1>The Evening That Never Ends</h1>
<p>You turn the mechanism toward memory. The lantern becomes a small eternal star, and Nera remains beneath its beautiful blue evening.</p>
<p>Everyone remembers the festival. No one gets to discover what comes after it.</p>
<p><strong>Ending: Stillness</strong></p>

:: EndingMorning [ending]
<h1>The First Sunrise</h1>
<p>You release the mechanism. The clock begins to move, slowly at first, then with the confidence of something that has waited a very long time.</p>
<p>Gold spills over the mountains. Nera sees morning for the first time in generations.</p>
<p><strong>Ending: The First Sunrise</strong></p>

:: EndingTogether [ending]
<h1>A Thousand Little Lights</h1>
<p>You share the lantern's light with the people. Every window, street, and rooftop glows as the city welcomes the future together.</p>
<p>The sun rises, but the people of Nera have learned that they can make light for one another, too.</p>
<p><strong>Ending: A Thousand Little Lights</strong></p>
